        "title": "Parcel 2: Issue with multiple export with same name",
        "body": "# \ud83d\udc1b bug report\r\n\r\nMultiple named exports with same name causes crash in parcel.\r\n\r\n## \ud83c\udf9b Configuration (.babelrc, package.json, cli command)\r\n\r\n\r\nRepro here: https://github.com/lindskogen/parcel-v2-repro\r\n\r\nBut basically this code snippet causes the bug:\r\n(The two exports named `faCircle`)\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--- If describing a bug, tell us what your babel configuration looks like -->\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport * as React from \"react\";\r\nimport { faCircle as farCircle } from \"@fortawesome/free-regular-svg-icons/faCircle\";\r\nimport { faCircle as fasCircle } from \"@fortawesome/free-solid-svg-icons/faCircle\";\r\nimport { FontAwesomeIcon } from \"@fortawesome/react-fontawesome\";\r\n\r\nexport interface Props {\r\n  text: string;\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const Header: React.FC<Props> = () => (\r\n  <h1>\r\n    <FontAwesomeIcon icon={farCircle} />\r\n    <FontAwesomeIcon icon={fasCircle} />\r\n  </h1>\r\n);\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n## \ud83e\udd14 Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nIt should bundle the code,\r\n\r\n## \ud83d\ude2f Current Behavior\r\n\r\n```\r\n@parcel/packager-js: Cannot read property 'buildError' of undefined\r\nTypeError: Cannot read property 'buildError' of undefined\r\n    at Scope.checkBlockScopedCollisions (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/scope/index.js:344:22)\r\n    at Scope.registerBinding (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/scope/index.js:501:16)\r\n    at Scope.registerDeclaration (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/scope/index.js:449:14)\r\n    at Object.Declaration (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/scope/index.js:125:12)\r\n    at NodePath._call (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/path/context.js:53:20)\r\n    at NodePath.call (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/path/context.js:40:17)\r\n    at NodePath.visit (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/path/context.js:88:12)\r\n    at TraversalContext.visitQueue (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/context.js:118:16)\r\n    at TraversalContext.visitMultiple (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/context.js:85:17)\r\n    at TraversalContext.visit (/Users/lindskogen/parcel/node_modules/@babel/traverse/lib/context.js:144:19)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## \ud83c\udf0d Your Environment\r\n\r\n<!--- Include as many relevant details about the environment you experienced the bug in -->\r\n\r\n| Software         | Version(s) |\r\n| ---------------- | ---------- |\r\n| Parcel           | 4a3f5349157\r\n| Node             | v10.17.0\r\n| npm/Yarn         | yarn 1.19.1\r\n| Operating System | macOS 10.15.1\r\n\r\n<!-- Love parcel? Please consider supporting our collective:\r\n\ud83d\udc49  https://opencollective.com/parcel/donate -->\r\n",
